    "ledger": [
      {
        "id": "E1",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "TorchNeuron: running HF models on AWS Trainium is easier than ever",
        "sourceUrl": "https://huggingface.co/blog/hf-torchneuron",
        "source": "Hugging Face Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-10-19T00:00:00.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-10-22T00:39:13.964Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E2",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "TorchNeuron provides a new native backend for PyTorch on AWS Trainium.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://huggingface.co/blog/hf-torchneuron",
        "source": "Hugging Face Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-10-19T00:00:00.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-10-22T00:39:13.964Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E3",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "Transformers, Diffusers and Kernels natively support it, making it easier than ever to run models on Trainium and to share them on the HF hub.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://huggingface.co/blog/hf-torchneuron",
        "source": "Hugging Face Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-10-19T00:00:00.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-10-22T00:39:13.964Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E4",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "TorchNeuron is a PyTorch plugin that brings a new backend for Trainium enabling support for eager mode, torch.compile and native distributed APIs like FSDP and TP.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://huggingface.co/blog/hf-torchneuron",
        "source": "Hugging Face Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-10-19T00:00:00.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-10-22T00:39:13.964Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E5",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "20, 2026, TorchNeuron will be available as a public beta.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://huggingface.co/blog/hf-torchneuron",
        "source": "Hugging Face Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-10-19T00:00:00.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-10-22T00:39:13.964Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E6",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "To date, the Hugging Face experience on AWS Trainium and Inferentia — AI chips designed respectively for cost-effective training and inference at scale — has been delivered through optimum-neuron .",
        "sourceUrl": "https://huggingface.co/blog/hf-torchneuron",
        "source": "Hugging Face Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-10-19T00:00:00.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-10-22T00:39:13.964Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E7",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "With TorchNeuron, 89% of the top 100 most-used text-generation model architectures are supported out of the box, compared to 46% with Optimum Neuron v0.4.5.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://huggingface.co/blog/hf-torchneuron",
        "source": "Hugging Face Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-10-19T00:00:00.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-10-22T00:39:13.964Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E8",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "The built-in asynchronous weight loading in Transformers is not supported on Neuron, so for now we disable it with HF_DEACTIVATE_ASYNC_LOAD=1 .",
        "sourceUrl": "https://huggingface.co/blog/hf-torchneuron",
        "source": "Hugging Face Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-10-19T00:00:00.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-10-22T00:39:13.964Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E9",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "TP_SIZE=4 FSDP_SIZE=8 HF_DEACTIVATE_ASYNC_LOAD=1 uv run torchrun --nproc_per_node=32 sft_neuron_example.py \\",
        "sourceUrl": "https://huggingface.co/blog/hf-torchneuron",
        "source": "Hugging Face Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-10-19T00:00:00.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-10-22T00:39:13.964Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E10",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "You can use for example this kernel to speed up your vision transformers with up to a x2.4 speedup on Trainium!",
        "sourceUrl": "https://huggingface.co/blog/hf-torchneuron",
        "source": "Hugging Face Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-10-19T00:00:00.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-10-22T00:39:13.964Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E11",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "Special thanks to the AWS team for their work on TorchNeuron and for their reactivity to our feedback to make the HF integration as good as possible.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://huggingface.co/blog/hf-torchneuron",
        "source": "Hugging Face Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-10-19T00:00:00.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-10-22T00:39:13.964Z"
      },
